1510 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 728 0 R
/E (Definition: APR stands for Annual Percentage Rate. It represents the total cost of borrowing on an annual basis, including interest rates and any additional fees or costs. The key difference between APR and your Interest Rate is accounting for fees. For a VA loan, comparing the APR to the Interest Rate helps borrowers understand the true cost of credit over a year. Two Lenders may offer the same Interest Rate but comparing the APR will show you which one has more in fees. In essence, it provides a clearer picture of how much you'll pay annually, beyond just the interest rate.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
